.th PASSWD I 11/4/78
.sh NAME
passwd \*- change login password
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd passwd
[ name [ old-password [ new-password ]]]
.sh DESCRIPTION
The
.it new-password
becomes associated with the given login name.
This can only be done by corresponding user
or by the super-user.
An explicit null argument ("") for either password
argument implies the null password.
.s3
If (either)
.it password
is not supplied, it will be requested (without echo) from
standard input.
An immediate reply of carriage return will denote the null password.
.s3
If
.it name
is not given,
the passwords requested will apply to the present real uid.
.sh FILES
/etc/passwd
.sh "SEE ALSO"
passwd (V), crypt (III), getty(VIII).
.sh BUGS
